CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Strongly Reciprocal

Preamble

CERN has developed this licence to promote collaboration among hardware
designers and to provide a legal tool which supports the freedom to use,
study, modify, share and distribute hardware designs and products based on
those designs. Version 2 of the CERN Open Hardware Licence comes in three
variants: CERN-OHL-P (permissive); and two reciprocal licences: CERN-OHL-W
(weakly reciprocal) and this licence, CERN-OHL-S (strongly reciprocal).

The CERN-OHL-S is copyright CERN 2020. Anyone is welcome to use it, in
unmodified form only.

Use of this Licence does not imply any endorsement by CERN of any Licensor or
their designs nor does it imply any involvement by CERN in their development.

1 Definitions

  1.1 'Licence' means this CERN-OHL-S.

  1.2 'Compatible Licence' means

    a) any earlier version of the CERN Open Hardware licence, or

    b) any version of the CERN-OHL-S, or

    c) any licence which permits You to treat the Source to which it applies
       as licensed under CERN-OHL-S provided that on Conveyance of any such
       Source, or any associated Product You treat the Source in question as
       being licensed under CERN-OHL-S.

  1.3 'Source' means information such as design materials or digital code
      which can be applied to Make or test a Product or to prepare a Product
      for use, Conveyance or sale, regardless of its medium or how it is
      expressed. It may include Notices.

  1.4 'Covered Source' means Source that is explicitly made available under
      this Licence.

  1.5 'Product' means any device, component, work or physical object, whether
      in finished or intermediate form, arising from the use, application or
      processing of Covered Source.

  1.6 'Make' means to create or configure something, whether by manufacture,
      assembly, compiling, loading or applying Covered Source or another
      Product or otherwise.

  1.7 'Available Component' means any part, sub-assembly, library or code
      which is used to Make a Product and which is not part of the Covered
      Source. Available Components may be commercially available or provided
      by third parties under any licence.

  1.8 'External Material' means anything (including Source) which is not part
      of the Covered Source but which is used to Make a Product or which a
      Covered Source references or calls upon.

  1.9 'Notice' means copyright, acknowledgement and trademark notices, Source
      Location references, modification notices (subsection 3.3(b)) and all
      notices that refer to this Licence and to the disclaimer of warranties
      that are included in the Covered Source. You may add other Notices as
      reasonably required by your licensing terms.

  1.10 'Licensee' or 'You' means any person exercising rights under this
       Licence.

  1.11 'Licensor' means a natural or legal person who creates or modifies
       Covered Source. A person may be a Licensee and a Licensor at the same
       time.

  1.12 'Convey' means to communicate to the public or distribute.

2 Applicability

  2.1 This Licence governs the use, copying, modification, Conveying of
      Covered Source and Products, and the Making of Products, in each case
      requiring that this Licence or a Compatible Licence is applied to the
      Covered Source in question.

  2.2 The Licensor irrevocably grants You the right to use, copy, modify and
      Convey Covered Source and make Products, subject to the conditions set
      out in this Licence.

3 Conditions

  3.1 You shall keep intact all Notices. All Notices shall be included in any
      Covered Source that You Convey.

  3.2 You may use any information in the Covered Source for any purpose
      without restriction.

  3.3 In addition to the obligations set out in subsection 3.1, if You
      Convey Covered Source or a Product based on it:

    a) You shall ensure that every recipient of the Covered Source has access
       to, and can access, any Available Component that is used in the
       Covered Source.

    b) You shall include a Notice in any Covered Source that You Convey
       stating that You have modified it, with the date and brief description
       of how You have modified it.

    c) You shall include a Source Location Notice in any Product based on the
       Covered Source and in any Covered Source that You Convey. This Notice
       may be placed in a prominent position, such as printed on a sticker or
       tag, or engraved or moulded into the Product.

    d) You shall license all Covered Source under this Licence (including any
       modification under subsection 3.3(b)) and all Products based on it
       under this Licence or a Compatible Licence.

4 Rights

  4.1 Subject to the terms and conditions of this Licence, each Licensor
      hereby grants to You a perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive, no-charge,
      royalty-free, irrevocable copyright licence to use, copy, modify, merge,
      publish, distribute, and/or sell copies of the Covered Source, and to
      permit persons to whom the Covered Source is furnished to do so,
      subject to the conditions of this Licence.

  4.2 This Licence does not grant You any rights to use any Licensor's or
      any Contributor's name, logo, or trademarks.

  4.3 Except as expressly stated in this Licence, this Licence does not grant
      any patent licence, nor is there any representation or warranty that the
      Covered Source does not infringe any patent or other intellectual
      property right.

